  message: "CAMPAIGN RUN, NOT CLEAN; the selector stays OFF. 89 faults planted (one statement each, 8 runs per shape sought), 43 stopped by the type gate, 46 ran, 40 failed a test: 3,729 failed tests, 3,544 kept by the selector, 171 named as ones coverage cannot speak for, 14 outside. By shape (ran / failed-a-test / outside): cached 6/5/0 (pool exhausted at 6), kept 8/6/11, fixture 8/8/1, state 8/6/0, child 8/7/0, plain 8/8/2. REPLAYED: 12 of the 14 are real misses in 2 faults, all in test_axiom_falsification.py: each fails alone (-n 0) with the fault and passes alone without it. Cause: the module-scoped fixture survey hands out a closure that keeps behavior maps in a dict, so only the first test per name records the analysis. Filed as INV-kazud (isbefore WI-pugol). The other 2 (pep508_name fault) did not reproduce in 4 tries (alone and in the 387-file set at -n 6, with and without the fault): added to WI-holuj as intermittent. Even a clean campaign of 40 runs would bound the per-run miss rate near 7% (95%), not prove it zero. Summary: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/bar/campaign3_summary.txt."  # 70e1
